    "priority_workload_id": "classic-1024x1024-b16-resident",
    "confidence_interval_supports_improvement": false,
    "representative_regression_percent": 112.77808707270904,
    "complexity_is_proportional": false,
    "rationale": "Rejected: a global four-tile chunk limit regresses every measured workload. Baseline is the existing 16-tile policy at 512 and 640, and the manual eight-tile workaround at 1024; the old 1024/16 configuration exceeded the existing allocation cap and has no valid timing. Separately retained a capacity fix: greedily take the largest ordered chunk below the existing Tier-1 per-allocation cap, without changing the requested tile limit or the cap. The 1024/16 case now completes as 11+5 in 208.74 ms, versus 205.60 ms for manual 8+8; no speedup claimed for this fix. Full nine-cell matrix, capacities, generator, command, executable hash, proof of the original allocation error and limitations in P27-P29-metal-optimization-notes.md."
  }
